Quantitative studies of the conductivity of electrolyte solutions help us understand the nature of chemicals in solution. Conductivity measurements can help us obtain chemical properties such as solubility or PH. The conductive properties of a solution depend on factors such as the nature of the solvent or solute and temperature. It depends ultimately on ionic mobility and the capacity of ions to carry electric charge.
This section addresses conductivity and how this property is measured in a chemistry laboratory.